Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mei: bus: restore nonblocking receive for callback consumers

MEI RX work notifications may coalesce when multiple messages complete
before the client callback runs. A callback that consumes messages needs
to drain the ready queue without waiting indefinitely on its final read.

Restore the nonblocking receive entry point, now needed by the IPTS client.
It uses the existing __mei_cl_recv() nonblocking path. This preserves the
current device lock, completion queue and ordinary-client flow control.
No existing API behavior changes and no vtag variant is needed by IPTS.

The API was removed as unused in commit 10d43ecbb012 ("mei: Remove unused
functions"). This is a new caller, not a regression caused by that removal:
IPTS used a single blocking read before and after that commit.

---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c b/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c
@@ -418,6 +418,20 @@
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mei_cldev_recv);
 
 /**
+ * mei_cldev_recv_nonblock - receive a pending client message without waiting
+ * @cldev: MEI client device
+ * @buf: buffer to receive
+ * @length: buffer length
+ *
+ * Return: bytes received, -EAGAIN if no message is pending, or another error.
+ */
+ssize_t mei_cldev_recv_nonblock(struct mei_cl_device *cldev, u8 *buf, size_t length)
+{
+	return __mei_cl_recv(cldev->cl, buf, length, NULL, MEI_CL_IO_RX_NONBLOCK, 0);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mei_cldev_recv_nonblock);
+
+/**
  * mei_cl_bus_rx_work - dispatch rx event for a bus device
  *
  * @work: work
diff --git a/include/linux/mei_cl_bus.h b/include/linux/mei_cl_bus.h
--- a/include/linux/mei_cl_bus.h
+++ b/include/linux/mei_cl_bus.h
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@
 ssize_t mei_cldev_send_timeout(struct mei_cl_device *cldev, const u8 *buf,
 			       size_t length, unsigned long timeout);
 ssize_t mei_cldev_recv(struct mei_cl_device *cldev, u8 *buf, size_t length);
+ssize_t mei_cldev_recv_nonblock(struct mei_cl_device *cldev, u8 *buf, size_t length);
 ssize_t mei_cldev_recv_timeout(struct mei_cl_device *cldev, u8 *buf, size_t length,
 			       unsigned long timeout);
 ssize_t mei_cldev_send_vtag(struct mei_cl_device *cldev, const u8 *buf,
